NOTICE
======

The AAR artifacts built from this subtree embed TWO native libraries, each for
three ABIs (arm64-v8a, armeabi-v7a, x86_64). Both are MIT-licensed, and MIT
requires its notice to accompany every copy — an AAR IS a copy.

  jabcode-sdk     jni/*/libjabcode-mobile.so
                  The JAB Code codec, compiled from src/jabcode/ in this repo.

  jabauth-client  jni/*/librabe_kem.so
                  The Rabe CP-ABE KEM, from src/main/jniLibs/. A Rust cdylib:
                  because it is statically linked, its whole crate tree is
                  compiled into the binary. The rabe crate (Bethencourt-Sahai-
                  Waters CP-ABE) is MIT; its ~50 dependencies are all permissive
                  (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2/3-Clause, Unlicense, BSL-1.0). No
                  copyleft licence appears anywhere in that tree. The full
                  per-crate table is maintained in the jab-auth-framework
                  NOTICE, generated from native/rabe-kem/Cargo.lock.

                  Note: the AAR previously committed under aar-artifacts/
                  predates these jniLibs and contains no .so at all, so an audit
                  of that stale artifact shows nothing to attribute. The
                  obligation appears on rebuild.

The MIT text below covers both.

